[Messages]
Coalition Representative: Hi, and thanks again for agreeing to support us on this issue. We just got formal notice that the committee hearing on the plastic bag fee ordinance is set for two weeks from now. The clerk’s office sent around the draft ordinance, an earlier staff memo, and a couple of studies from other cities.

Coalition Representative: Our members definitely have concerns, but in this setup we’re looking to you mainly as a nonpartisan explainer. Before we get into any strategy, we’d like to send Councilmember Garcia and Garcia’s policy aide a short, neutral briefing from us that helps everyone get on the same page about what this proposal does and what the evidence says.

Coalition Representative: Could you please draft a concise memo—no more than two pages—that we can email to Garcia’s office? It should:
- Clearly state that it’s prepared on behalf of the Local Retailers Coalition;
- Briefly describe the draft ordinance and how the fee would work in practice at checkout;
- Summarize, in balanced fashion, what the research and other cities’ experiences suggest about environmental outcomes, city revenues, and impacts on different types of retailers and customers;
- Flag the main tradeoffs and a couple of plausible design options (e.g., exemptions, phase-in, or alternatives) without taking a position.

Coalition Representative: Please avoid advocating for or against the fee in this memo—Garcia’s office is already getting a lot of spin, so we think a straightforward, well-sourced overview from us could actually be helpful. We’ll share your draft only with Councilmember Garcia and Garcia’s aide. Let me know if you need any clarification on our local retail context before you start drafting.
